{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1376505-what-happens-to-regular-clothes-when-shifting","id":1376505,"title":"What happens to regular clothes when shifting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-25T04:16:03-07:00","id":1376505,"title":"What happens to regular clothes when shifting?","content":"I've been getting really into Werewolf lately (mostly because of the Bastet) because its really freaking awesome- but I have one question.. What happens to clothes that aren't patterned for transformations when changing? Lets say your fighting in an alley after sensing a Bane nearby in the Umbra, does your regular clothes entirely shred into pieces? Do you have to sneak around naked in the city to avoid being seen after side-stepping back into the material world? I know some specifically made Fera attire attune with your transformations, but what about your regular clothes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T05:09:49-07:00","id":1376521,"title":"","content":"If you don't attune to your clothes they get Shredded when you grow, and they tangle you when you just become lupus. They also may not go with you when you step sideways. Your clothes may stay with you if you step sideways and don't attune them, but it seems equipment may be left behind, been a while for me to remember the specifics. But you can Attune say a backpack or have something like Magpie's swag Fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T10:11:19-07:00","id":1376576,"title":"","content":"Non-dedicated clothing is subject to the normal laws of physics, which is bad for your clothing if your shape-shifting.<br /> <br /> Non-dedicated clothing doesn't go into the Umbra with you (though some people interpret this slightly more harshly and say you have to strip first rather than your non-dedicated stuff being left behind). But it's not destroyed, so if you cross back where you started, they'd still be there baring outside interference.<br /> <br /> If your character can't dedicate clothing or attune a Fetish that would help, plan on dealing with nudity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T00:44:29-07:00","id":1376682,"title":"","content":"Edit: &quot;There\u2019s a level 1 fetish to solve this problem.&quot; &lt;-- I cant find this fetish anymore. Must have been in a splat book.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's still a level 1 rite to solve this problem still.<br /> Rite of Talisman Dedication Level One. You can use your gnosis to dedicate your clothes to all forms. More items if you have a higher score. Requires work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":19533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","user":"Pnizzle","date":". 03-26-2020, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T18:46:58-07:00","id":1376760,"title":"","content":"Magpie's Swag is a Level 1 Fetish that's in W20 core that helps with this as noted above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T04:47:26-07:00","id":1377494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pnizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1376505-what-happens-to-regular-clothes-when-shifting?p=1376682#post1376682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: &quot;There\u2019s a level 1 fetish to solve this problem.&quot; &lt;-- I cant find this fetish anymore. Must have been in a splat book.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's still a level 1 rite to solve this problem still.<br /> Rite of Talisman Dedication Level One. You can use your gnosis to dedicate your clothes to all forms. More items if you have a higher score. Requires work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Magpie's Swag (Level One, Gnosis 5), in the W20 Core Page No 221.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T07:41:09-07:00","id":1377511,"title":"","content":"Oh. This is like for items in a bag. (Discount bag of holding). <br /> <br /> There was like a necklace I remember that you wore and it allowed you to absorb your clothes and items. Only the necklace remained. It was real long ago. I can\u2019t remember. Getting old I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T01:17:31-07:00","id":1377901,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that there has to be some kind of angle here for a Glasswalker Theurge fashion mavin who specializes in designer clothing Fetishes and Talans. But I am weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:44:42-07:00","id":1377970,"title":"","content":"No you right, a Glass Walker theurge as a fashion designer would make a lot of sense given how clothing and accessories that won't threaten the veil are something every garou needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T12:59:30-07:00","id":1378023,"title":"","content":"I mean, fashion designer is something a low Rage Garou could do as a job, but there's no particular benefit to it. A Glass Walker can take an tailored (probably by a kin) Armani suit and use Talisman Dedication on it to be styling in Homid and Glabro (possibly even Crinos).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T01:52:40-07:00","id":1378211,"title":"","content":"Make it a ring and it could be like Barry Allen\u2019s flash suit ring. Haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T02:00:59-07:00","id":1378214,"title":"","content":"Some additions from the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Fetishes need attunement, but it seems that this can be done by any garou, even without knowledge of the Rite of Talisman dedication. Rules seem to indicate, that the attunement process is a dialogue with the spirit/bane in the fetish and shall be role-played.<br /> <br /> As of revised, it is encouraged, that the limit of dedicated items (permanent gnosis) shall not be enfrorced harshly as one set of normal clothes shall count as one item, &quot;using&quot; one Gnosis.<br /> <br /> The non-dedicated items shall not enter the umbra should not be circumvented by dedicating a backpack and puting the stuff in it. W20's Magpie feitsh bag is a huge thing, because before this fetish was introduced, one would have to perform a rite. Dedicating certain items, like technology, was reducing renown (except for Glass Walkers) and the only means to bring stuff in the umbra was the Tractor Beam gift (rank 4), which was discontinoued in W20, although the effect was included into Grasp of the Beyond, iirc.<br /> <br /> For the most cases, I personally, would allow jewlery as part of the normal set of clothes, too, if it isn't magical and stuff, but I would see a wallet and all the credit cards and ids in there as a separate item. But there were topics in this forum discussing this before.<br /> <br /> As for shapeshifting:<br /> revised introduced a size alteration rite for equipment in TB CoG rev, but I'd assume most people include that property in the Talisman dedication.<br /> <br /> Belts, or other sturdy materials, and especially shackles might prohibit shap-shanging, make it intensly painful or cause inquiries. There is, to my knowledge, no force given, that a human body expanding to Crinos size can bring to bear. But if one is tied to something with a metal chain multiple times, it probably isn't bursting. Same goes for crawling in small spaces. Failing a frenzy check while in an office building air vent, one is probably ripping the thin sheet metal, but if it happens in an underground sewer made of concrete surrounded by earth, the garou probably isn't just stuck, but will also suffer broken bones...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}